claim.claim-text:
a substrate film (102) having a first side and an opposing second side;
electronics comprising at least one light source (110), optionally a LED (light-emitting diode), provided upon the first side of the substrate film and a number of electrical conductors (112), preferably printed electronics based electrical conductors, at least electrically coupled to the at least one light source (110), the at least one light source (110) being configured to emit light at least in selected one or more frequencies or wavelengths, optionally including visible light;
an optically transmissive element (104) comprising thermoplastic optically transmissive, having regard to the selected frequencies or wavelengths, material having a first refractive index, said optically transmissive element preferably comprising optically transmissive thermoplastic material molded onto the first side of the substrate film (102) so as to at least partially embed the at least one light source (110) therewithin; and
optical cladding (106, 106a, 106b, 106d, 106e, 106f) comprising material having a lower refractive index than the first refractive index and provided adjacent the optically transmissive element, wherein the optical cladding comprises several layers, wherein at least one layer of the optical cladding extends essentially parallel to a surface direction of the substrate film and at least one further layer (106e) of the optical cladding extends essentially parallel to a transverse direction of the substrate film.
wherein the at least one light source, the optically transmissive element and the optical cladding have been mutually configured (702, 704) so as to convey light emitted by the light source (110) within the optically transmissive material of the optically transmissive element, at least portion of the conveyed light undergoing a substantially total internal reflection when incident upon the optical cladding.

obtaining (504) a substrate film (102) configured to accommodate electronics on at least first side thereof, said film having the first side and a second side;
providing (508) electronics comprising at least one, optionally printable or mountable, light source (110) such as LED upon the first side of the substrate film and a number of electrical conductors (112), preferably by printed electronics technology, connecting to the at least one light source (110);
establishing (510), preferably through molding or casting, an optically transmissive element (104) onto the first side of the substrate film and thereby at least partially embedding the at least one light source, the transmissive element being established from thermoplastic optically at least translucent, preferably transparent, material having a first refractive index, and
wherein in the method, it is also established (518), optionally through printing, dip coating, spraying and/or at least partially jointly with the substrate film, optical cladding (106) to locate adjacent the optically transmissive element, said optical cladding comprising material having a lower refractive index than the first refractive index, comprising establishing several layers of the optical cladding, such that at least one layer of the optical cladding extends essentially parallel to a surface direction of the substrate film and at least one further layer (106e) of the optical cladding extends essentially parallel to a transverse direction of the substrate film.
